  CX: status | One-line success receipt. THREE PARAMETERS, all supplied by the screen: {action} is a stable CODE (created, completed, reopened, added, updated, removed, deleted) and never a rendered word — the catalogue turns it into the verb; {subject} is the BARE NAME of the thing acted on (user text, never a phrase such as 'milestone X', because a phrase composed in one language cannot be ordered or inflected by another); {kind} is a stable CODE for WHAT the subject names (project, milestone, other). Each locale supplies its own noun and its own word order — English verb-first, French naming the thing first with the participle last — which is why the action arms are repeated inside every kind arm: a locale has to be free to move the verb. other catches an unknown kind or an unknown action code. Ends with a full stop.
